Source: ps3-system
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Maintainer: Tiberiu Chibici <chibicitiberiu@gmail.com>
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13)
Standards-Version: 4.7.2
Rules-Requires-Root: no

Package: ps3-system
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, systemd, systemd-sysv, openssh-server, udev, util-linux, kmod, python3, whiptail, alsa-utils
Recommends: bluez, network-manager
Description: PS3 system configuration (Linux on the PlayStation 3)
 Wired networking (systemd-networkd), SSH host keys on first boot and SSH logins (password or
 key, never root), the /dev/ps3gpu_* nodes, swap (zram, and the disk swap behind spare VRAM from
 ps3rsx), a larger free-memory reserve, NetworkManager kept off the wired port, DualShock 3
 pairing over USB, and the apt sources (Debian ports plus Walnut's signed suites, with pins that
 keep the PS3 kernel and Mesa), ps3-gameos-mount (GameOS's disk, read-only, on demand),
 walnut-bugreport, and OpenAL Soft's output as 16-bit (/etc/xdg/alsoft.conf). Replaces the files the
 image used to write (archived in /var/backups on upgrade).